    "body": "## Purpose\n\nSGLang exposes `POST /parse_function_call`, which runs the server's tool parser over text that the caller already has. This adds the same endpoint to vLLM.\n\nIt is useful whenever model output is parsed outside the chat-completion path: an agent loop that owns its own turn structure, an RL rollout harness, or a disaggregated deployment where the generate tier returns text that still has to be turned into tool calls (cf. the derender RFC #42729).\n\n## Design\n\n- `tool_call_parser` in the request body selects the parser; when omitted, the server's `--tool-call-parser` is used.\n- The parser instance is built with the served tokenizer and the requested `tools`, so parsers that resolve argument schemas keep working.\n- Response shape matches SGLang: `{\"normal_text\": ..., \"calls\": [...]}`.\n- Missing/unknown parser returns a 400 `ErrorResponse`; nothing is generated, so the endpoint never touches the engine.\n\n## Tests\n\n`tests/entrypoints/unit_tests/test_parse_function_call.py` covers explicit and server-default parser selection, text without a tool call, and both error paths. The tests build their own FastAPI app, so they need no GPU or running server.\n",
